{"baseRefName":"fix/lifecycle-lows","baseRefOid":"dfac31be4b28f9bd6695c79e6bde2dc5a17ad9f5","body":"## Summary\n\nStacked on #544 (fix/lifecycle-lows). Final batch of the shell-UX lows.\n\n- `terminal-mouse.ts` now strips non-SGR mouse reports — X10 (`ESC[M`+3 bytes) and urxvt (`ESC[Cb;Cx;CyM`) — including partial sequences held across stdin chunks. A terminal left in legacy tracking, or one ignoring DECSET 1006, previously fed those payload bytes to Ink as garbage keypresses.\n- `bootstrap-intent.ts` emits a `flag-ignored` diagnostic when a parsed flag has no reader in the selected launch: `-t` without `-i`, `--jump` without `-S`, `-a` with `-y`, `-S` shadowed by a resolvable `-i`, `--download-path` without `--download`, and `-t` on namespaced ids. Rendered on stderr and in `--dry-run` output.\n- Width gates and truncation in the preview rail, calendar model, settings page builder, ink-shell option labels, and setup screens now use `measureColumns()`/`padColumnsEnd()` — a 20-char CJK title is 40 terminal columns, and `.length` math let it overflow the rail untruncated.\n\n**Dead session actions**: verified already handled — `PlayerServiceImpl` retires non-reusable sessions before `play()`, `PersistentMpvSession.play()` rejects when dead, and `PlayerControlServiceImpl` catches per-action command failures. No change warranted.\n\n**Not in this batch** (feature-sized, to be filed as issues): unicode glyph fallback across the shell (~85 sites, no capability layer exists), SR-channel support.\n\n#### Test plan\n- [x] `bun test` focused shell UX set — 36 pass / 0 fail\n- [x] Affected gate green on push — 26 tasks, 5974 unit + 296 integration, 0 fail\n- [x] `verify:doc-paths` — all paths resolve","files":[{"path":".docs/download-offline-onboarding.md","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":".docs/mobile-terminal-runtime.md","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":".docs/provider-dossiers/miruro.md","additions":1,"deletions":1,"ch